ah  yes champion  that i got the top of the oven should be  a little bit warmer but the real test is  judging the pie according to richard's  56 point pizza evaluation rubric that  means when a guest takes a bite of this  it's not going to fall apart it's not  going to fall apart okay beautifully  baked structurally sound pizza  and the flavors of fermentation  should be real floral and  complex looks really good yeah and  crushed it  richard's pizza obsession had a  bittersweet beginning it started during  a post-college graduation trip to italy  i tasted this food that was so fantastic  and better than any pizza or pasta that  i've ever tasted so you come back from  italy and it's like your everything is  opened up your taste buds everything  opened up but also closing down as soon  as i got back my mom was  very sick and i remember crying on the  airplane home because  i was just off this adventure right and  i knew that it wasn't  it wasn't going to end well  robin richer died of cancer in 2002.  richer says he got through his grief by  channeling his mom's work ethic as he  attempted to recreate the tomato sauce  he tasted in italy so i made batch after  batch after batch  and  i started visiting farmers markets to  buy the ingredients and that's where i  really  it just all clicked it's the ingredients  it really comes down to ingredients and  technique eventually richer raised  enough money to buy a failing restaurant  where he worked at perfecting pasta  before turning his attention to pizza  but pizza is alive it's a living  breathing thing until it's consumed  because  what makes pizza pizza is that it's  bread so i started studying bread making  and learning about fermentation so we  have to understand the science in order  to create a really amazing pizza  on a consistent basis in 2012 richer  opened ratsa serving up artisanal pizza  so good it soon earned this headline in  the new york times the best pizza in new  york is in new jersey it was important  because it broke through the location  factor if you put me in arizona or  arkansas i'm gonna make fantastic pizza  because your location does not dictate  its merits richer made us some of that  fantastic pizza like the project  hazelnut with hazelnuts from blight  resistant trees developed by his alma  mater rutgers university i love this  next the fungi featuring chanterelle and  maitake mushrooms we have a forager that  we work with he just brings us a certain  quantity of mushrooms whatever  danbot isn't that good oh my god  the guancha is richer's love letter to  rome yeah we sat with  a piece of guanchali a caliper which is  a measuring device for  very specific thicknesses we cut 12  different size pieces and we got just  the right one so that  the edges get a little bit crispy but  the bottom of it stays a little pliable  the perfect saltiness too it's a journey  in taste much like the creation has been  for richer he writes this of pizza in  his book no other food is so perfect in  its imperfections so forgiving on its  way to mastery and the joy is in the  journey for me of creating whatever that  people learning and meeting people along  the way this is a flower miller a wheat  grower a mushroom forager a cheese maker  we just put it together your obsessions  keep channeling to new things  what's the next obsession after pizza or  does it stay with pizza there's always  something to learn in the process  always it's never going to be finished  until i shut this restaurant down  and i hope he never shuts the restaurant  down the pizza's delicious it doesn't  obviously i can't get it here meatballs  are wonderful also and he recreates the  taste from italy and this chickpea salad  so do enjoy that because i love you all  i loved crushed yeah crushed red pepper  which is delicious  good stuff  we will be right back  [Music]  for those of you still with us you get  to watch us eat um this book actually i  really want to say what's amazing about  it i've tried making pizza with my  stepson with jack and it's hard  sometimes and it was what dan said you  you think you can understand words but  this has qr codes so you can actually  see the videos to it and look at this  yeah with his daughter that's cool oh  that's so adorable isn't it oh look  signed book signed book for all of you  oh wow  dana thank you  you know also one thing at his pizzeria  and i know a lot of places do this but  it's really about local ingredients for  him as often as he can  and he touched on this a little and  saying that it's the journey but  he likes the fact that he has a cheese  maker that's nearby and he doesn't just  get the cheese from him he then sees  other restaurants using that cheese this  cheese and you're helping that that area  anything that's fresh  anything that you can get that to him is  a good ingredient it is just so great a  lot of times on saturday right after the  show i'll take my son to a pizza place  and we have our  weekend  together and it's just like a great i  mean oh jeff yeah it's like a bar it's a  pizza bun fantastic yeah yeah i just  love the headline the best pizza i know  did you throw the  red pepper in the chickpeas nice wow  the best pizza in new york is in  new jersey so we have to take a trip  there because i couldn't bring it it  wouldn't be fresh enough can we finally  take a trip  can we talk more  with more food in our mouths  and it's just so good for everybody  let's officially clink oh yeah cheers  say it cheers to cheers cj oh yeah happy  birthday happy birthday my dog one day  belated but yeah  yeah you come over here thank you just  throw the glasses at each other so you  can clean  we will be right back and stick around  oh yeah

